{"availability":"available","full":"YusufCeng1z/svelte-bash","name":"svelte-bash","description":"A fully typed, lightweight, and customizable terminal emulator component for Svelte 5. Features a virtual file system, custom commands, themes, and autoplay mode for demos. 🚀","category":"Other","language":"Svelte","stars":100,"forks":2,"created":"2025-12-10T04:13:29Z","updated":"2026-06-24T04:29:12Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://svelte-bash.netlify.app/","topics":["bash","cli","command-line","console","frontend","shell","svelte","svelte-5","svelte-component","terminal","terminal-emulator","typescript","ui-component"],"demo":"https://svelte-bash.netlify.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-06T09:40:20.711Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-06T09:40:20.711Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-06T09:40:20.711Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-06T09:40:20.711Z","stars":100,"forks":2}],"technologies":["Svelte"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Svelte Bash is a high-performance terminal emulator component designed specifically for modern Svelte applications. It provides a realistic shell experience with a virtual file system, command history navigation, and advanced features like autoplay sequences for tutorials.","Note: As of v1.0.1, svelte-bash has been refactored to use Pure Vanilla CSS internally. This means it has ZERO dependencies on Tailwind CSS and will render correctly in any project (including Bootstrap, Tailwind, or plain CSS projects). You do NOT need to install Tailwind.","Whether you are building a developer portfolio, a documentation site, or a web-based CLI tool, Svelte Bash offers the perfect balance of aesthetics and functionality."],"features":["Lightweight & Fast: Zero external dependencies, 4kb gzipped.","Virtual File System: Fully functional ls -la, cd, cat, and pwd commands.","Filesystem Mutation: Create, move, copy, and delete files/folders (mkdir, touch, rm, cp, mv).","Persistent State (v1.2): Built-in persist prop t